{
  "_meta": {
    "status": "active",
    "purpose": "Capability descriptors for the One-Brain Coach Orchestrator. Each capability is a pure Brain module with a declared input contract (requires/optional), dependency edges (depends_on), and output keys (produces). The Orchestrator reads this to run the right modules in dependency order WITHOUT containing any coaching rule.",
    "spec": "docs/COACHING_CONTRACTS_SPEC.md §2",
    "note": "requires/optional draw ONLY from input_keys (state- or intent-derived). depends_on references capability ids. produces is declarative output documentation (its own namespace; NOT validated against input_keys). The resolver computes the transitive closure of depends_on, then topo-sorts.",
    "ladder": {
      "purpose": "Each capability's honesty is the nine-rung completion ladder in `ladder`, NOT a single self-declared status (retired 2026-07-21, Phase 2 Work item 3, closes H-05/H-15 'manifest overstates capability'). The full assessment and rung definitions are published in docs/CAPABILITY_COMPLETION_LADDER.md.",
      "rungs": ["built", "unit_tested", "runner_wired", "inputs_available", "route_consumed", "user_visible", "validator_covered", "live_proven", "owner_accepted"],
      "rules": [
        "Monotonic ladder: a higher rung may not be true while any lower rung is false (validated by services/capabilityManifest.js). A capability's honest position is the highest contiguous rung it reaches.",
        "Understate when unsure: when a capability is genuinely ambiguous between two rungs, the lower one is assigned — understating is safe; overstating is the disease (owner ruling 2026-07-20).",
        "Name the consumer: no capability may claim route_consumed or higher without a non-empty `consumer` naming the live route/seam that consumes it (validated here).",
        "Evidence for route_consumed/live_proven: a capability at route_consumed or live_proven must carry an `evidence` array of linked test or trace ids — enforced by Drift Guard 4 (scripts/check-completion-ladder.js, npm run check:ladder).",
        "owner_accepted is owner-gate only: no agent may ever self-assign owner_accepted=true; it is set solely at an explicit owner gate (owner ruling 2026-07-20)."
      ],
      "runtime": "The Orchestrator (services/coachOrchestrator.js) treats ladder.built===false exactly as the retired status:'missing' did — the capability is skipped-with-flag (never dropped), and its build-ahead module file need not exist yet."
    }
  },
